WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.940
SpaceX will attempt to catch both the super heavy booster and starship upper stage on flight 15. A dual catch would be the first full recovery of an orbital launch vehicle. This is SpaceX Daily Episode 137. Quarterly results, Tesla merger committees, and a vandenberg scrub follow, then the counterpoint, the ai front, and the engineering deep dive. Flight 15 is expected next month, and the launch tower arms are assigned to both stages, according to KeepTrack.space.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.680
An 82nd animation from the earnings webcast showed the Starship Upper Stage finishing its

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:40.260
belly flop, steering with forward and aft flaps at the nose and tail, then swinging vertical.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.380
The arms grab it after the upper stage drops past the tower top.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.200
Elon Musk said the first try is more likely than not to work.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.160
SpaceX is keeping Starship flights coming through the end of the year if that try fails.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.515
Gwynne Schottwell described SpaceX's third quarter results in which connectivity kept

00:00:58.515 --> 00:01:00.875
climbing and Starship started to haul more.

00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:08.715
The company reported $14.6 billion of revenue, a 161% rise from the same quarter last year.

00:01:09.295 --> 00:01:15.515
The connectivity segment posted 69% revenue growth and 99% growth in income from operations,

00:01:16.035 --> 00:01:19.455
helped by enterprise, government, and consumer starlink adoption.

00:01:19.455 --> 00:01:24.715
Shotwell said Starship Flight 14 delivered 26 Starlink version 3 satellites.

00:01:25.155 --> 00:01:30.495
Those satellites provide roughly 10 times the downlink capacity of a Falcon 9 Starlink launch.

00:01:31.135 --> 00:01:36.355
The service was active across 174 markets, with hundreds of thousands of additional

00:01:36.355 --> 00:01:42.530
enterprise and aviation customers. SpaceX and Tesla each set up a special committee of independent

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:49.830
directors to study a possible merger. Elon Musk called the combination a good idea on the

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:57.430
space reports. He cited shared work in superintelligence software, chip design, the TeraFab facility, robotics,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:03.690
master orbit via the Star-Mine constellation and connectivity. Musk said he supports combining

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:08.410
the two largest companies. He stated there is a lot of merit to combining them as they are

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:14.810
pretty much in the superintelligence singularity. The review follows SpaceX acquiring XAI in February

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.350
and going public in June.

00:02:17.414 --> 00:02:22.154
Vandenberg Space Force Base scrubbed a planned Falcon 9 Starlink launch after a technical

00:02:22.154 --> 00:02:22.574
issue.

00:02:23.094 --> 00:02:24.314
Spaceflight now reports.

00:02:24.974 --> 00:02:31.094
The mission was to carry 27 Starlink satellites on October 20th, using a booster on its 36th

00:02:31.094 --> 00:02:31.354
flight.

00:02:31.874 --> 00:02:37.594
It is now targeted for a window opening at 2.59pm Pacific time on October 21st.

00:02:38.134 --> 00:02:41.634
The booster is slated to land on the drone ship a shortfall of gravitas.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:48.474
That would be landing number 229 for that ship, and Falcon Booster landing number 673.

00:02:49.074 --> 00:02:54.254
The rocket will fly on a southeasterly trajectory, and roughly 8.5 minutes after liftoff,

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.434
the booster will target the drone ship if the attempt proceeds.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:04.700
Star-links launched and working counts were updated again, per KeepTrack.space, 13,000

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:12.040
satellites have been launched, 11,154 are in orbit, and 11,140 are operationally

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:17.680
in low-earth orbit. SpaceX added 1.6 million subscribers in the third quarter,

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:23.000
10 upcoming Starlink conjunctions, meaning predicted close approaches appear in

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.600
the current Socrates collision probability list, and none of them reach high risk.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.460
Two of those 10 carry upstream numbers that are physically implausible, so they

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:37.360
are treated as stale or erroneous reports. Two Starlink satellites also have

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:43.564
reactive reentry predictions. Elon Musk posted on X asking for honest feedback from GROC and

00:03:43.564 --> 00:03:49.104
Fable on technical topics. The post directs people to the bot interface for direct interaction.

00:03:49.764 --> 00:03:53.184
Observers noted the emphasis on practical engineering questions.

00:03:54.216 --> 00:03:59.836
Highway 101 Southbound in California showed up in a reddit photo of what appears to be a Falcon 9

00:03:59.836 --> 00:04:05.876
capsule, which is not confirmed. Commenters speculated on whether it was a recovered dragon capsule

00:04:05.876 --> 00:04:10.875
or a test article. NASA Space Flight outlined a busy launch week

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:14.775
spanning California, Florida, New Zealand, Japan, and China.

00:04:15.475 --> 00:04:19.955
Nine rockets are on the schedule, including SpaceX's trio of Falcon 9 missions.

00:04:20.675 --> 00:04:25.555
The same preview flag, Jax's H3 debut and Rocket Lab's electron flight.

00:04:26.215 --> 00:04:29.155
Analysts noted the high cadence across multiple providers.

00:04:30.204 --> 00:04:35.224
One thing worth watching is the roughly $1 billion SpaceX spent on Starship in the

00:04:35.224 --> 00:04:40.244
third quarter. Alongside its first quarter as a public company that was solidly profitable.

00:04:40.864 --> 00:04:46.524
Net income was $4.4 billion. Earnings materials shown nameplate compute capacity,

00:04:47.024 --> 00:04:53.064
the labeled peak draw of the installed machines, at 1.7 gigawatts as of September 30th,

00:04:53.304 --> 00:04:56.164
while Starship remains the primary capital consumer.

00:04:56.864 --> 00:05:02.224
Sustaining that investment with a planned $35-40 billion fourth quarter capital expenditure

00:05:02.224 --> 00:05:08.024
run rate, we'll test whether AI and connectivity revenue can scale fast enough to support continued

00:05:08.024 --> 00:05:10.344
hardware iteration without eroding margins.

00:05:11.391 --> 00:05:17.071
On the AI front, SpaceX added $6.7 billion dollars year over year from superintelligence

00:05:17.071 --> 00:05:23.531
solutions and infrastructure, KeepTrack.Space Reports, Cloud Services Agreements, the acquisition

00:05:23.531 --> 00:05:28.641
of Cursor, and growth in superintelligence models and software applications, including

00:05:28.641 --> 00:05:30.441
rock, drove that increment.

00:05:31.021 --> 00:05:35.421
Public filings now place most expected future revenue in AI-related business.

00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:40.841
The company described the AI segment as overtaking starlink on some internal contribution

00:05:40.841 --> 00:05:42.121
measures during the quarter.

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:46.181
AI business revenue surged 830% in the quarter.

00:05:47.214 --> 00:05:52.174
For that flight 15 upper stage catch, the engineering reality is converting hypersonic

00:05:52.174 --> 00:05:57.894
high drag flight into a vertical capture only seconds before contact: the flaps steer the belly-flop, then the Raptor engines relight to flip the stage upright and brake.

00:05:57.894 --> 00:06:02.594
fact. Those flaps have to raise pitch and yaw while the starship upper stage is still

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:07.314
moving at hundreds of meters per second. A few hundred milliseconds of timing error puts

00:06:07.314 --> 00:06:13.294
it outside the arm geometry envelope. Horizontal velocity and leftover rates have to die to roughly

00:06:13.294 --> 00:06:18.654
a meter and a degree, while the stage is still on aerodynamic control. The upper stage

00:06:18.654 --> 00:06:24.454
has no super heavy style grid fins, and body flap bite collapses below a few kilopascals

00:06:24.454 --> 00:06:29.814
of dynamic pressure. That pressure is 1.5 times air density times velocity squared.

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:36.354
Near the ground, density is about 1.2 kilograms per cubic meter. At 100 meters per second,

00:06:36.554 --> 00:06:43.014
you get on the order of 6 kilopascals. At 50 meters per second, you get about 1.5 kilopascals.

00:06:43.454 --> 00:06:48.134
Authority falls with the square of speed, so the flaps go mushy faster than the vehicle

00:06:48.134 --> 00:06:52.134
slows. Right into the flip. That square law is why the last

00:06:52.134 --> 00:06:57.974
second is the whole game. Hypersonic means faster than Mach 5 on the order of a kilometer

00:06:57.974 --> 00:07:03.774
and a half per second or more, before drag bleeds it down. At vertical residual horizontal

00:07:03.774 --> 00:07:09.034
speed must sit under 1 meter per second and pitch and yaw rates under 1 degree per second,

00:07:09.494 --> 00:07:15.214
or the arms and the skirt yield. 2 meters per second is not twice the problem. Energy and

00:07:15.214 --> 00:07:20.934
therefore load go with velocity squared, so it is 4 times the hit. 1 extra degree per

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:24.354
second walks a compressive stack into a peel on the arm pins.

00:07:24.974 --> 00:07:29.874
Structural steel yields on the order of a few hundred megapascals, so a side slip at

00:07:29.874 --> 00:07:32.674
remaining descent speed is a spike, not a tap.

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:38.254
The plan uses body flaps rather than engines for those last seconds, which keeps a plume

00:07:38.254 --> 00:07:42.814
off the tower and makes the catch a purely mechanical take of a tiny leftover state.

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:47.314
The controller trims that burn into the last half-second before capture.

00:07:47.314 --> 00:07:52.954
At 40 meters per second of descent, that half-second is on the order of 20 meters of travel.

00:07:53.314 --> 00:07:58.354
The arms are a fixed geometry and cannot chase a miss, so the vehicle has to fly into

00:07:58.354 --> 00:07:59.674
a box measured in meters.

00:08:00.334 --> 00:08:05.314
Ground tests cannot stack reentry heat soak, falling dynamic pressure, and flight mass

00:08:05.314 --> 00:08:10.074
properties in one article, so the first attempt is the first combined margin data.

00:08:10.694 --> 00:08:14.274
Expendable upper stages have always been the accepted waste in this business.

00:08:14.274 --> 00:08:19.334
the shuttle orbiter bought reuse with wings and a runway and paid for it in dry

00:08:19.334 --> 00:08:24.034
mass. Repeatable starship upper stage recovery would drop a second heat shielded

00:08:24.034 --> 00:08:28.494
system and the propellant otherwise spent discarding the stage. The idiot

00:08:28.494 --> 00:08:32.534
index of a thrown away ship, the finished article over stainless sheet and

00:08:32.534 --> 00:08:37.594
methalox stays high until you catch it. Dual use flaps must survive peak

00:08:37.594 --> 00:08:42.254
heating and still provide pitch in low dynamic pressure so the design wants more

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:47.934
area and faster actuators than re-entry steering alone would ever need. On the tape, the stock

00:08:47.934 --> 00:08:54.710
finished lower by a little over 7%. Before we go, the Vandenberg Falcon 9 still has an October

00:08:54.710 --> 00:09:03.750
21st window. That covers everything worth knowing about SpaceX today. SPC-X is trading at $147.79

